Name: Roboto Font
Short Name: roboto-classic
URL: https://github.com/googlefonts/roboto-classic
Version: N/A
Date: 2026-10-13
Update Mechanism: Static (https://crbug.com/584037521)
License: OFL-1.1
License File: OFL.txt
Security Critical: no
Shipped: no

Description:
Licensing and origin metadata for the Roboto font subset and Incremental Font
Transfer (IFT) patches used by IftPatcherTest in
third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fonts/ift/ift_patcher_test.cc and
IftCustomFontDataTest in
third_party/blink/renderer/core/css/ift_custom_font_data_test.cc.

The test fixture files reside in the parent directory (testing/data/) because the
relative patch URLs are embedded directly within the font binary:
- third_party/blink/renderer/platform/testing/data/roboto-ift.ttf
- third_party/blink/renderer/platform/testing/data/roboto-ift.woff2
- third_party/blink/renderer/platform/testing/data/04.1.ift_gk
- third_party/blink/renderer/platform/testing/data/04.2.ift_gk
- third_party/blink/renderer/platform/testing/data/08.1.ift_gk
- third_party/blink/renderer/platform/testing/data/08.2.ift_gk
- third_party/blink/renderer/platform/testing/data/0C.1.ift_gk
- third_party/blink/renderer/platform/testing/data/0C.2.ift_gk
- third_party/blink/renderer/platform/testing/data/0G.ift_tk
- third_party/blink/renderer/platform/testing/data/0K.ift_tk
- third_party/blink/renderer/platform/testing/data/0O.ift_tk
- third_party/blink/renderer/platform/testing/data/0S.ift_tk
- third_party/blink/renderer/platform/testing/data/10.ift_tk
- third_party/blink/renderer/platform/testing/data/14.ift_tk
- third_party/blink/renderer/platform/testing/data/18.ift_tk
- third_party/blink/renderer/platform/testing/data/1C.ift_tk
- third_party/blink/renderer/platform/testing/data/1G.ift_tk
- third_party/blink/renderer/platform/testing/data/1K.ift_tk
- third_party/blink/renderer/platform/testing/data/1O.ift_tk
- third_party/blink/renderer/platform/testing/data/1S.ift_tk

Local Modifications:
Derived from Roboto[wdth,wght].ttf by generating a mixed-mode IFT encoding.
The base font supports codepoint 'a', feature 'smcp' (GSUB table; glyph outlines
are in a glyph-keyed patch), and design space wght [100, 400]:
- 04.1.ift_gk / 04.2.ift_gk: outline for 'b' (initial / expanded wght).
- 08.1.ift_gk / 08.2.ift_gk: outline for 'c' (initial / expanded wght).
- 0C.1.ift_gk / 0C.2.ift_gk: outlines for 'smcp' glyphs (initial / expanded wght).
- 1K.ift_tk: tables for 'b', applied to the base font.
- 1O.ift_tk: tables for 'c', applied to the base font.
- 1S.ift_tk: tables for wght [500, 900], applied to the base font.
- 14.ift_tk: tables for 'c', applied after 1K.ift_tk.
- 1C.ift_tk: tables for 'b', applied after 1O.ift_tk.
- 0G.ift_tk, 0K.ift_tk, 0O.ift_tk, 0S.ift_tk, 10.ift_tk, 18.ift_tk,
  1G.ift_tk: remaining transitions in the table-keyed extension graph for {'b',
  'c', wght [500, 900]}.

The font also contains an unmapped padding glyph (gid 7). The encoder always
keeps the last glyph in the base font, so the padding glyph prevents 'a.smcp'
(gid 6) from being pulled into the base font.

The IFT encoding was generated with an internal build of the IFT encoder, using
roboto-ift-plan.txtpb in this directory. The public equivalent is
https://github.com/w3c/ift-encoder, which provides the same font2ift tool:

  pyftsubset 'Roboto[wdth,wght].ttf' --text=abc --gids=591 \
    --layout-features+=smcp --output-file=roboto-abc-pad.ttf
  mkdir out
  font2ift --input_font=roboto-abc-pad.ttf --plan=roboto-ift-plan.txtpb \
    --output_path=out/ --output_font=roboto-ift.woff2
  woff2_decompress out/roboto-ift.woff2  # Produces out/roboto-ift.ttf.

- Roboto[wdth,wght].ttf is available at
  https://github.com/google/fonts/tree/main/ofl/roboto. Glyph 591 is an
  unmapped simple glyph that sorts after the 'smcp' glyphs (588..590).
- With the public encoder, font2ift can be built and run from the ift-encoder
  repository with `bazel run -c opt //util:font2ift -- <flags>`. Output from
  the public encoder may not be byte-identical to the checked-in files.
- pyftsubset is part of fontTools. woff2_decompress is part of
  https://github.com/google/woff2.
- font2ift always writes WOFF2, so roboto-ift.ttf is decompressed from it.
